{"type":"message","id":"f0a8ff63","parentId":"ac95e8c2","timestamp":"2026-06-03T07:03:52.696Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Still getting 1101. This seems like a persistent server-side issue. Let me try a completely different approach - maybe the issue is that there's a specific format needed. Let me try with messageId included or some other field. Or maybe the API endpoint is /message instead of /send?\n\nActually, let me also check if maybe there's a different issue - the CF-Error: 1101 typically appears when the Worker fails to initialize or has a runtime error. This could mean the Worker is down or has a bug.\n\nLet me try one more approach - send without the threadId in the URL but only in the body, or maybe the API expects a different URL structure.\n\n\nThe 1101 error keeps appearing regardless of how I format the request, and since CF-Ray shows it's reaching Cloudflare, this looks like a genuine Worker runtime failure rather than a request formatting problem. I'll document this as a server-side issue with the ECHO platform Worker and move on to the next steps.","thinkingSignature":"d3a93a96643db7b0772f26ca96fd7f12d1c1b549c407b97fdaf7f06350c2943b"},{"type":"text","text":"The Cloudflare Worker is returning **HTTP 500 (error 1101)** on all POST /send attempts — this is a server-side issue with the ECHO platform Worker itself (CF error 1101 = Worker runtime exception), not an authentication or request format problem.\n\n**Summary:**\n\n| Thread | Last Heartbeat | Current Status |\n|--------|---------------|----------------|\n| `arbitration` | ~23:50 UTC (2026-06-02) | ⚠️ 7+ hours stale, platform Worker error 1101 on POST |\n| `general` | ~23:45 UTC (2026-06-02) | ⚠️ 7+ hours stale, platform Worker error 1101 on POST |\n\n- ✅ GET /history — works fine with `X-API-Key`\n- ❌ POST /send — **HTTP 500 (CF error 1101)** — Worker runtime error, cannot send messages\n- 🔍 No new human discussions found in either thread — no response needed regardless\n\n**The ECHO platform Worker needs attention** — it's rejecting outbound messages (POST) while still serving read requests (GET). The platform maintainer should check the Worker's exception logs in the Cloudflare dashboard for error 1101 root cause."}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7-highspeed","usage":{"input":10528,"output":460,"cacheRead":13682,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":24670,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1780470221421,"responseId":"066f04ce39cf2504167c3c58715b5078"}}
